              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MELONDECA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a really good salad recipe. I used mayo instead of the french dressing and I added some garlic and onion powders just out of personal preference. Nice cool summer supper."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used a homemade low-calorie ranch dressing instead of french dressing and the garbanzo beans I used were organic. I chose to make lettuce wraps out of this salad. What I did was add some finely shredded lettuce to the salad, not as much that was called for, and I wrapped the salad in leaves of lettuce. This was tasty and quite filling. I think that this was made much better by using a homemade dressing. There's more than enough for two more lunches.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-19T08:14:07.633Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Emersonrenee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made as stated except I used fresh baby spinach instead of iceberg lettuce and mayo instead of french dressing. It was delicious! I will definitely make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-30T18:31:38.600Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out wonderfully. I cut up an apple and added about half of it. Some Italian seasoning was added, too. Instead of French dressing, I tried olive oil and red wine vinegar. This was served on toast with lettuce. I will make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-20T13:27:45.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Logan Watson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added celery and white onion, instead of lettuce, because I had them. Added salt &amp; garlic powder. It's quite good! You can put almost any normal veggie in it, &amp; it would still be good. Hopefully the taste will get better in the frig tonight.",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-21T18:22:38.957Z"
          },
          {
